Revision 0.1.5
Coral - server development language

0.1.5 changes:
It is no longer necessary to define the server type (require = files).
New native libraries: CORS, STORAGE 

Logic and syntax

port - Defines the port on which the server will run.
create - It defines whether it will be https or http.
rec - receive request
ret - return response
require - defines the modules to be used in the server
index = defines the default page of the server
. - define what to do next
$ - create a function
file - receive file
save - save data or files
progress - receives the current value of a task being executed and returns
true
false
wait.end - wait end of the process
"" - returns text
// - comments



simple examples:

just a simple server:

require = CORS
create.http <rec, ret> = [
  ret "Resposta do servidor"
    ret.end]
port {3000}

Hosting an HTML page:


create.https <rec, ret> = [
  index = "home.html"
    ret.index] 
port {3001}


download page:


create.https <rec, ret> = [
  index = "myapp.html"
    ret.index] 

$ download (
rec {/download.html}
ret 'my-app.apk'
ret.end)

port {3002}


Upload files to a specific directory:

create.https <rec, ret> = [
  index = "myapp.html"
    ret.index] 

$ upload (
rec {api/upload}.get 
get{file.filename, file.size}.save = storage{D:\mydrive\files} //D:\ is an external drive, the STORAGE library facilitates dynamic file allocation.
get.upload progress.wait.end
if complete
ret "File saved successfully!"
if incomplete
ret "An error ocurried while uploading"

ret.end)

port {3003}
